    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Recently redecorated, this bright and spacious apartment has been thoughtfully upgraded with both the main bathroom and ensuite recently refurbished to a high standard. Offering generous accommodation, excellent privacy and a superb balcony, No108 is an ideal choice for those seeking a turnkey home in one of North Dublin`s most sought after locations.\n\nThe accommodation begins with an entrance hallway featuring attractive light laminate flooring, a generous cloakroom and a convenient hot press. The recently renovated main bathroom is finished with contemporary tiling and comprises a bath with overhead shower, WC, wash hand basin, heated towel rail, recessed mirror with feature lighting and an extractor fan.\n\nThe heart of the home is the bright open plan living, dining and kitchen area. The spacious living room enjoys a feature fireplace and large picture windows which fills the room with natural light while opening onto a generous private balcony. The balcony enjoys excellent privacy with no overlooking properties and offers pleasant views across the mature trees, railway station and towards the entrance of Malahide village.\n\nThe adjoining dining area flows seamlessly into the fully fitted galley style kitchen, complete with an integrated oven and hob, dishwasher, fridge freezer and washer/dryer. A range of floor and wall mounted units together with recessed spot lighting provide both practicality and style.\n\nThe principal bedroom is a generous double room featuring extensive built-in wardrobes, continued laminate flooring and a beautifully refurbished fully tiled ensuite incorporating a shower cubicle, WC, wash hand basin, heated towel rail and fitted mirror.\n\nThe second bedroom is another spacious double room with fitted wardrobes, excellent natural light and the same peaceful outlook towards the balcony and mature trees.\n\nFurther enhancing this impressive apartment is gas fired central heating, a recently painted interior, quality flooring throughout and a superb balcony with ample space for outdoor dining and entertaining.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall\nL shaped with access to all rooms. Wood flooring, storage press, entryphone and inset spotlights.\n\nOpen Plan Living / Dining / Kitchen\n\nKitchen\nRefurbished with floor and wall mounted units, built in over and hob with splashback. Integrated appliances include, fridge/freezer, dishwasher and washer/dryer. Inset spotlights to ceiling.\n\nDining Area\nConveniently placed opposite the kitchen with ample space for a dining table.\n\nLiving Room\nOpen plan with feature gas fire, wood flooring, patio doors giving access to the private balcony.\n\nBalcony\n\nBedroom One\nWith range of built in wardrobes, access to the ensuite.\n\nEnsuite\nRecently refurbished fully tiled with large shower, WC, wash hand basin, heated towel rail and recessed mirror with shelf and feature lighting. Inset spotlights to ceiling\n\nBedroom Two\nWith built in wardrobe, access to the balcony.\n\nBathroom\nRefurbished, fully tiled with white suite comprising bath, WC, wash hand basin, heated towel rail and recessed mirror with feature lighting. Inset spotlights to ceiling.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Well-presented second-floor apartment </li><li> Recently redecorated throughout </li><li> Two recently refurbished bathrooms </li><li> Large private balcony with excellent privacy </li><li> Built in wardrobes to both bedrooms </li><li> Gas fired central heating </li><li> Parking </li><li> Short stroll to Malahide village, DART station, restaurants, cafés and every local amenity</li></ul>"
      },
